<title>EGYPT: Egyptian 91-day Treasury bill yield falls.</title>
<headline>Egyptian 91-day Treasury bill yield falls.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.722 on Wednesday from 9.765 percent at the previous auction on March 26.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 600 million pounds and accepted bids for 673.1 million, rejecting bids for 182.175 million. Bills worth 610.900 million mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The central bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: July 3, 1997 (June 26, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.722 percent (9.765)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 673.100 million (665.300 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 954.275 million (1,223.650 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.249-9.787 percent (9.493-9.804)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.249-10.099 percent (9.493-10.099)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 119 (124)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 170 (186)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
